---
import '../styles/site.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const siteUrl = 'https://stressless-grasp.github.io';
const asset = (path: string) => `${base}/assets/${path}`;
const figures = [
  { file: 'method-v4.png', label: 'Method overview', text: 'Stress-aware demonstration generation, point-cloud policy learning, and real-world deployment.' },
  { file: 'teaser.png', label: 'Stress-aware grasping', text: 'The latest teaser figure from the manuscript.' },
  { file: 'evaluation-latest.png', label: 'Evaluation set', text: 'Eleven fragile and deformable object categories used in real-world evaluation.' },
  { file: 'training-latest.png', label: 'Training set', text: 'Real demonstrations used for the comparison policies.' },
];
const results = [
  { name: 'StressLess (ours)', lift: .67, safe: .78, score: .73 },
  { name: 'RGB-finetune', lift: .48, safe: .67, score: .58 },
  { name: 'RGB-scratch', lift: .57, safe: .67, score: .62 },
  { name: 'Point-cloud DP', lift: .43, safe: .67, score: .55 },
  { name: 'RGB-frozen', lift: .18, safe: .53, score: .36 },
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>StressLess: Gentle Grasping from Stress-Aware Demonstrations</title>
    <meta name="description" content="StressLess learns generalizable gentle grasping from stress-aware demonstrations generated in simulation." />
    <meta property="og:title" content="StressLess: Gentle Grasping from Stress-Aware Demonstrations" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="A stress-aware planner and point-cloud policy for fragile and deformable objects." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" /><meta property="og:url" content={`${siteUrl}/`} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={`${siteUrl}/`} /><link rel="icon" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="wrap site-header"><a href="/">StressLess</a><nav><a href="#method">Method</a><a href="#results">Results</a><a href={asset('paper/stressless.pdf')}>Paper (PDF)</a></nav></header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="wrap intro">
        <p class="kicker">ROBOT LEARNING · RESEARCH PROJECT</p>
        <h1>Generalizable gentle grasping<br /><i>from stress-aware demonstrations.</i></h1>
        <p class="lede">StressLess uses a finite-element stress objective to synthesize demonstrations at scale, then learns a single point-cloud policy that transfers to fragile and deformable objects in the real world.</p>
        <p class="authors">Anonymous authors · Double-blind submission</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={asset('paper/stressless.pdf')}>Read the paper</a><a href="#method">See the method ↓</a></div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap facts" aria-label="Project facts">
        <div><strong>34</strong><span>simulated object categories</span></div><div><strong>6k+</strong><span>stress-aware demonstrations</span></div><div><strong>11</strong><span>real-world evaluation categories</span></div><div><strong>275</strong><span>real-world evaluations</span></div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap section" id="method">
        <div class="section-title"><p class="kicker">01 · METHOD</p><h2>Plan with stress.<br />Learn with breadth.</h2></div>
        <p class="body-copy">A distributed-pad contact model and soft-body FEM surrogate score candidate grasp poses and closing widths. Randomized pose, size, shape, and material produce over 6k demonstrations across 34 categories without human tele-operation. A single point-cloud diffusion policy observes one external depth camera and robot proprioception; no tactile or force feedback is used.</p>
        <div class="image-frame method-pdf"><object data={asset('figures/method-v4.drawio.pdf')} type="application/pdf" aria-label="StressLess method overview"><p>Your browser cannot display the PDF inline. <a href={asset('figures/method-v4.drawio.pdf')}>Download the method figure (PDF)</a>.</p></object></div>
        <div class="contributions"><h3>Contributions</h3><ol><li>A stress-aware grasp planner that selects both grasp location and closing width for deformable items.</li><li>A single policy spanning diverse fragile and deformable categories from point-cloud observations alone.</li><li>A 275-trial real-world evaluation across categories and variations in pose, size, and shape.</li></ol></div>
      </section>
      <section class="band" id="results"><div class="wrap section"><div class="section-title"><p class="kicker">02 · RESULTS</p><h2>Lift objects.<br /><i>Keep them intact.</i></h2></div><p class="body-copy">Real-world scores are averaged across 11 categories and two evaluators. Lift is normalized lift height; Safe is a lift-conditioned damage score; S-Lift averages both.</p><div class="score-row"><div><strong>0.67</strong><span>Lift</span></div><div><strong>0.78</strong><span>Safe</span></div><div><strong>0.73</strong><span>S-Lift</span></div></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Mean real-world performance (55 trials per method)</caption><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Lift ↑</th><th>Safe ↑</th><th>S-Lift ↑</th></tr></thead><tbody>{results.map((r, i) => <tr class:list={{ ours: i === 0 }}><th>{r.name}</th><td>{r.lift.toFixed(2)}</td><td>{r.safe.toFixed(2)}</td><td>{r.score.toFixed(2)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="note">StressLess also retries: 25 of 31 first-attempt failures were retried, recovering 10 lifts and contributing 0.18 to the overall Lift score.</p></div></section>
      <section class="wrap section"><div class="section-title"><p class="kicker">03 · FIGURES</p><h2>Across simulation<br />and reality.</h2></div><div class="figure-grid">{figures.map((f) => <figure><a class="image-frame" href={asset(`figures/${f.file}`)}><img src={asset(`figures/${f.file}`)} alt={f.label} loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption><h3>{f.label}</h3><p>{f.text}</p></figcaption></figure>)}</div><div class="downloads"><a href={asset('figures/method-v4.drawio.pdf')}>Download method figure (PDF)</a><a href={asset('figures/Eval objects-colored.pdf')}>Download evaluation figure (PDF)</a></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap"><span>StressLess · Anonymous submission</span><span>Project materials for double-blind review</span></footer>
  </body>
</html>
